  "notes": "How Loud Is a Fire Alarm Test?\n\nFire alarms are designed to be impossible to ignore. But how loud is one when you are actually standing in the building?\n\nThis SPL Reference measurement captures a routine fire alarm test in a real indoor environment, recording both the alarm itself and the surrounding sound before and during its activation.\n\nThe result provides a real-world reference for the sound level and short-term exposure produced by an emergency warning system, rather than a laboratory measurement of the alarm device.",
